tasha: Heads-up, PR https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/498 added a troubleshooting entry for 429/timeouts but reviewers requested a compact, testable snippet that shows context trimming + Retry-After handling. Can someone draft?

liam: I can do a short Go example and a tiny TypeScript one. Key things: honor Retry-After, short bounded retries, deterministic trimming (don't drop system prompt), then fallback to a cheaper model or cached result.

nina: Agree. Also call out when to abort vs when to retry (timeouts vs 429). Timeouts -> likely network or backend slowness; 429 -> rate limits. We should show AbortController in JS and context length check in Go.

liam: Draft TS:```ts
// TS: retry 2x, respect Retry-After, then fallback
async function genWithFallback(payload){
  for(let i=0;i<2;i++){
    const res = await fetch('/v1/generate', {method:'POST', body:JSON.stringify(payload)});
    if(res.status===200) return res.json();
    if(res.status===429){
      const ra = res.headers.get('Retry-After');
      const waitMs = ra ? Number(ra)*1000 : Math.pow(2,i)*500;
      await new Promise(r=>setTimeout(r, waitMs));
    } else break; // non-retryable
  }
  // deterministic trim: keep system + last 2 user turns
  payload.input = trimHistory(payload.input, 2);
  return fetch('/v1/generate?model=small-1',{method:'POST', body:JSON.stringify(payload)}).then(r=>r.json());
}
```

tasha: Good. Add one line reminding devs to test trim behavior with eval prompts so instructions aren't removed. Also mention caching layer as an optional fast-path for frequent queries.

liam: Got it. Go snippet:```go
// Go: bounded retries, trim if still 429
func CallWithFallback(ctx context.Context, client *redwood.Client, req redwood.Request) (*redwood.Response, error) {
  for i:=0;i<2;i++ {
    resp, err := client.Generate(ctx, req)
    if err==nil && resp.StatusCode==200 { return resp, nil }
    if resp!=nil && resp.StatusCode==429 {
      time.Sleep(time.Duration(math.Pow(2,float64(i))) * 500 * time.Millisecond)
      continue
    }
    break
  }
  // trim: keep system prompt + last N turns deterministically
  req.Input = TrimHistory(req.Input, 2)
  req.Model = "small-1"
  return client.Generate(ctx, req)
}
```

